Subject: [PATCH] djihads-frag-barrier: defer the 3D fragment barrier to the next draw that reads the pass (EDEN_UP_DJ_FRAG_BARRIER=1)

djihads-frag-barrier: defer the 3D fragment barrier to the next draw that reads the pass (EDEN_UP_DJ_FRAG_BARRIER=1)

Ported from Djihads80/Eglantine nx2-experimental c6d2acd37 ("nx2: Ocarina of Time stability,
shader and performance fixes", #794, Nx2Perf fragment_barrier, from #161; on by default there),
GPL-3.0-or-later: RasterizerVulkan::FragmentBarrier, the scheduler's barrier state
(fragment_barrier_state.h folded into vk_scheduler.h), GraphicsPipeline::writes_storage and the
draw-side test, TextureCache::SamplesRenderTarget. Co-authors per that commit.

The 3D engine's fragment barrier (method 0x0DE0) ended the render pass at once; the pass end
carries the barrier. Upstream measured Ocarina of Time ending ~5,900 render passes a second
there. With the switch the barrier is noted while a pass is open, and the next draw ends the pass
only if it samples an image bound as a render target (colour or depth) or a draw of the pass
writes storage buffers, images or global memory; otherwise the pass goes on. The note clears
whenever the pass ends for any other reason (compute, copies, a new framebuffer, a submit).
Both draw paths test it: ConfigureImpl and EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW's ConfigureDelta.
Review fixes (2026-11-09, not upstream; both only end a pass where T82 ended one):
- A barrier that arrives while no pass is open but a deferred clear waits (DeferColorClear,
  DeferDepthStencilClear; used by default) is pending too. T82's barrier realized that clear
  before the next draw; upstream's version let a draw that samples the cleared target land in
  the clear's own pass, with no barrier after the load-op clear.
- DrawTexture (Maxwell draw_texture) samples its source without the draw-side test: with a
  barrier pending it ends the pass first, as T82 did.
Off (unset): byte-identical commands (writes_storage is noted but only read with the switch).

Checks (djihads-c6d2_checks.sh, log djihads-c6d2.checks.log): git apply --check on the T82 core,
patch on a copy, prepare-vulkan-port.py same 6 anchor skips as baseline, -fsyntax-only rc=0 on
every TU the diff reaches (generated copies included), injected static_assert seen in each,
and all four djihads-*.diff stack in one tree (same anchors, rc=0). Not built, not run.
Re-run after the review fixes: review-djihads-c6d2/rv_checks.sh (+ rv_stack_parallel.sh, on top
of fritchii-relocate-v2, its reloc guard, fritchii2-grhand/copybarrier/bankflag/writemark), same
results.

